# Static IDs for every account a recipe in the image creates through
# useradd.bbclass (USERADDEXTENSION = "useradd-staticids", conf/distro/proximos.conf).
#
# /data outlives the rootfs and its files keep numeric owners, so an account that
# lands on another number in the next image loses its own /data tree - which is
# what dynamic allocation does to every account after one that is added or
# removed (issue #92). These are the numbers main images allocated dynamically up
# to 2026-09, so units already in the field keep theirs.
#
# Never renumber a line. A new account takes a number no line uses yet; a removed
# account keeps its line, so its old number is never handed to another account.
# Only name, uid and gid are pinned: the empty fields keep whatever the recipe
# passes to useradd. The group of the same name is in proximos-group.
